#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065324} :activity/id #uuid "80148d75-f74f-5156-96a5-7a61c7ad871b" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048657 :topic/id #uuid "b2fc29cc-ac54-53dd-a9d9-2df302336f43" :topic/math-academy-id 367} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065181 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064292 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064135 :question/id #uuid "6818c8ab-41e3-546d-a427-304316324bf0" :question/math-academy-id "e-7829"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa831011-1184-5d09-b4e8-b1192443d1b5" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064701} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064703}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Rate of Change of a Shadow's Length Using Similar Triangles and Negative Rates"} :step/id #uuid "8cd418cf-566e-5476-9114-f2cd4d0ee2f5" :step/math-academy-id 29097} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065324 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065386 :tutorial/content "Suppose that Bob, who is $1.8 \\,\\text{m}$ tall, stands in front of a $3\\,\\text{m}$ street light. How fast does the length of Bob's shadow change if he walks *away* from the street light with a speed of $0.5\\,\\text{m/s}$?\n\n![](images/1b/1bd1bc069863b0b54381e6c9c641a6a5eadd16dccd8a5bf153f47fe88342dc94.png)\n\nWe can solve problems like this using three simple steps.\n\n**Step 1:** Draw a diagram and identify the variables that change with time.\n\n![](images/fa/facdffb79b65e027853464df3f6216fbde7fe3b5619b549aff1010924297b5c4.png)\n\nIn the above diagram, we have denoted the following:\n\n- $x$ is the distance between Bob and the street light\n- $y$ is the length of Bob's shadow\n\nBoth $x$ and $y$ change with time as Bob walks away from the light. In particular, we're told that Bob's velocity is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}= 0.5\\,\\text{m/s}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}\n$$\n\nis positive. This is because the distance between Bob and the street light increases as Bob walks away from the light.\n\nOur goal is to calculate\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Write down an equation that relates $x$ and $y$.\n\nFrom our simplified diagram, we see that we have two right triangles that share a common angle. Therefore, they are similar by the AA (angle-angle) criterion for similar triangles.\n\nSince the two triangles are similar, the ratios between the corresponding sides are equal. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x + y}{3} &= \\frac{y}{1.8} \\\\\n1.8x + 1.8y &= 3y \\\\\n1.8x &= 1.2y \\\\\n18x &= 12y \\\\\ny &= 1.5x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Differentiate with respect to time and plug in the known values.\n\nWe use the chain rule to differentiate the above equation with respect to time. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dt}(y) &= \\frac{d}{dt}(1.5x) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dt} &= 1.5 \\cdot \\frac{dx}{dt}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the known value of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t} =1.5\\cdot (0.5) = 0.75 \\, \\text {m/s}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of Bob's shadow increases at a rate of $0.75 \\, \\text {m/s}$." :tutorial/id #uuid "39868416-9b99-584e-912c-55bb370a34c1" :tutorial/math-academy-id 495 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "a20a71f6-b2d9-5750-9e9f-3902758d5232" :step/math-academy-id 923 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065325}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065325 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064384 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064028 :question/id #uuid "69ba4325-7189-590d-95dd-b11487b632c8" :question/math-academy-id "e-230"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c8eb340e-8c49-5478-8cca-a340e9a266e3" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048214} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049658} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050978}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064657} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064727}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Rate of Change of a Shadow's Length Using Similar Triangles"} :step/id #uuid "003dba43-750d-5a17-857a-cc7a3e864193" :step/math-academy-id 924 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065181}}] :activity/title "Calculating Related Rates Using Similar Triangles" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186064453}]}
